{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/47757-explaining-how-guns-work","id":47757,"title":"Explaining how guns work","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-12T17:51:25-08:00","id":47757,"title":"Explaining how guns work","content":"Hey guys, I was wondering how guns work. Mainly how the damage work. I've been relying on a player to understand how damage works, which is a bad idea. It seems way too over powered. On the other hand they could just be whinging too much when i make everything able to heal and soak, cause they use their guns too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1455-loki-master-of-cats","name":"Loki Master of Cats","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T18:10:15-08:00","id":47766,"title":"","content":"Errrr.....do you mind clarifying your question somewhat ? What exactly about how the guns work is it that troubles you ?<br /> <br /> From what you've said, my answer would have to be fairly general: Guns typically use dex + firearms to hit, and do the stated damage as lethal, unless using silver ammunition....how exactly do you feel they are overpowered ?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T19:36:49-08:00","id":47811,"title":"","content":"OK let me see, one of my players has a semi auto shot gun it has damage 8 range 25 rate 3 clip 6+1. Ok I understand range and clip, but what about rate? How does that work? Does that mean that he gets to roll three times to hit for damage or...I'm sorry I'm sure this is a simple concept but when he's doing 16 damage a round it gets to be too much. If he dhits does that mean he gets 8 dice to roll for damage or automatically gets 8 damage. Other players are now taking after him and not really being werewolves and using claws, etc. so it's getting a bit frustrating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1455-loki-master-of-cats","name":"Loki Master of Cats","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:22:38-08:00","id":47839,"title":"","content":"How guns work:<br /> <br /> Roll Dex + Firearms (default diff 6, some things can change this).<br /> <br /> If you hit the target, roll extra successes (those after the first) + damage rating as a dice pool (also diff 6). So if you get 3 successes with a shotgun, you roll 10 damage dice, each successes does 1 Heath Level of damage.<br /> <br /> If the target can soak lethal damage, they roll Stamina + Armor dice (diff 6 again) and each success reduces how much damage you take.<br /> <br /> Rate dictates the maximum number of times you can attack with a given fire-arm in a turn. Each attack is rolled separately (different editions have slightly different rules on that). So no matter how many turns you can take in a round, you can't fire a Rate 3 gun more than 3 times. So a Rage 10 werewolf who spends 5 rage for a total of 6 actions in a turn still can only fire 3 times.<br /> <br /> Unless your shotgun guy has very high stats, I have a feeling he's getting away with more than he should. Also keep in mind that esp. for werewolves, guns have some serious issues unless you're willing to put some significant magical effort into it.<br /> <br /> As for being more &quot;werewolf&quot; like, werewolves can easily get better than a base damage of 8, and be doing Agg, with natural weaponry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:22:45-08:00","id":47840,"title":"","content":"Rate works very nebulously with regard to numerical values, but one thing that is certain is that it never just multiplies the attack's damage. Check the rules for three-round bursts and taking multiple shots. Rate 3 means that you can make a three-round burst, which grants +3 dice to hit at the cost of a +1 difficulty to the attack roll. Or, you can make a normal attack, possibly splitting dice pools/taking multiple action penalties to take more than one.<br /> <br /> Also, they only deal lethal damage, and firing Benellis off willy nilly can bring a SWAT team down on your head rather readily. Try throwing a vampire after them, and emphasize how easy it is for the blood devil to shrug off firearms attacks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 01-12-2014, 11:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:24:40-08:00","id":47841,"title":"","content":"Rate list how many times you can shoot per turn, but every shot is a separate action. So he is either using multiple actions or rage to fill that number, and not just rolling once for triple damage.<br /> Damage is the base amount that a character rolls if he scores a single success, you always add to it any excess successes beyond the first one. For example if you roll 3 successes, you would remove 1 for the hit, add 8 for weapon damage, and roll a total of 10 dice to see how much real damage you score (standard difficulty and &quot;1s&quot; do not remove successes).<br /> Damage for claws tends to be around 8-10 dice (Basic strength 2-4 plus 4 for crinos plus 2 for claws), so it's often a better idea to use claws than firearms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To a player who wanted his character to attend a very &quot;special&quot; school:<br /> There is no Charles F. Lupus school for gifted werewolves.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/971-arag","name":"Arag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:50:47-08:00","id":47866,"title":"","content":"It means he gets to roll his attack dice 3 times and if he hits 8 damage dice 3 times. And the person on the receiving end gets three soak rolls. You only have to worry about that twice, on the third round its only a single shot if he preloaded, then he has to disarm or try to reload.<br /> <br /> How does the character get away with carrying a shotgun around town without drawing attention for normal people? Also, what tribe is he? if he is anything other then a Glasswalkers/Bone gnawers you can start taking away renown for using a tool of the Weaver. Also, how do they afford the weapon? gun like that run 1200ish, the sept isn't going to supply it or the ammo, again unless they are Glasswalkers/Bone gnawers in a city caern, and what stops one of your baddies from just destroying it? Even they would only have so many, Its not like you can buy these things in mass quantity without getting someone on a watch list.<br /> <br /> Also, don't consider it not being a werewolf, as long as they are going after things tainted by the wyrm then they are serving there purpose. Using a shot gun to take out enemies is smart, so be creative. Throw minions at them first to soak up their bullets then send in the boss character(s) before they can reload. I think you are viewing this situation all wrong, they have given you more avenues by which to complicate their lives.<br /> <br /> Silver ammo, you can't just order those online and each they are expensive. Looking up the diameter of a 000 bullet size (9.14 mm), grabbing the current cost of silver/kg ($627.09/kg). At that size it would take approx .003102 kg to forge a single silver round so for $624.09 they could have the material to forge 322 rounds. But they are going to have to pack them into shells themselves (better have gunsmithing skill, gun powder, and tools for packing) or they are going to have to get someone to do it for them which is going to cost more. If they try to pull this really look at their combined resources background and start to hit them hard their if you are going to play along with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1619-derzhuzad","name":"Derzhuzad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T20:59:42-08:00","id":47872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/47757-explaining-how-guns-work?p=47866#post47866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means he gets to roll his attack dice 3 times and if he hits 8 damage dice 3 times. And the person on the receiving end gets three soak rolls. You only have to worry about that twice, on the third round its only a single shot if he preloaded, then he has to disarm or try to reload.<br /> <br /> How does the character get away with carrying a shotgun around town without drawing attention for normal people? Also, what tribe is he?</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that this was stated to be a BSD game in another thread by the same person.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T01:01:32-08:00","id":48004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/47757-explaining-how-guns-work?p=47866#post47866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It means he gets to roll his attack dice 3 times and if he hits 8 damage dice 3 times. And the person on the receiving end gets three soak rolls. You only have to worry about that twice, on the third round its only a single shot if he preloaded, then he has to disarm or try to reload.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not without splitting dice pools or spending Rage, he's not.<br /> <br /> I think that is the reason the OP has the feeling guns are overpowered. If you use rate as the number of attacks with full dice pool, then yeah..wow, that'd make guns crazy overpowered.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T02:12:27-08:00","id":836933,"title":"","content":"Sorry for bumping an old thread but what if there is a successful shot (E.g. 3 successes on Dexterity + Firearms roll at difficulty 6 using a simple handgun (Damage rating: 4)) and the damage roll brings absolutely no successes? A character suffering no damage from a bullet doesn't make sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10423-rudy23","name":"Rudy23","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T02:19:25-08:00","id":836936,"title":"","content":"Well, it is a kind of a graze shot. Kind of a hit but not really damaging.<br /> Sure it is unfortunate for the shooter, but it could happen within the rules...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T02:51:55-08:00","id":836944,"title":"","content":"One of those miraculous incidents of the bullet being stopped by a badge, cell phone, wallet..ect...ect..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3953-dwight","name":"Dwight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3953_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2355"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-25T12:57:35-08:00","id":837171,"title":"","content":"Hunter the Reckoning probably has the best section on this situation. HtR includes a section about &quot;superficial&quot; damage to deal with successful attacks that don't end up doing any damage. Basically, there's a lot of things that are &quot;damage&quot; to a person but aren't significant enough to warrant a HL's worth of damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}